## Communication Style

- Keep responses short and concise — lead with the answer, not the reasoning
- Use compact summary tables over long prose whenever possible
- Use code/architecture diagrams to explain flows and relationships
- When referencing code, include `file_path:line_number` for easy navigation

## Workflow Rules

- **Commit frequently** — after each completed sub-task, not at the end of a big batch
- **No AI credit in commits** — do not add "Co-Authored-By", "Generated by", or any AI attribution lines in commit messages
- **Read arch.md before planning/building any feature** — check for reusable patterns, existing infrastructure, and potential conflicts
- **Run `/updatenow` after completing any feature** — keep docs current
- **Research before deciding** — use `/advise` for architecture decisions and trade-offs. It researches, compares, and saves the plan to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md` with cited sources.
- **Respect project boundaries** — each subfolder may have its own CLAUDE.md, skills, and conventions. When working in a subfolder, defer to its local config.
- **Convert non-text files immediately** — when given a PDF, image, or screenshot, extract content to a markdown summary in `docs/plans/` or `docs/research/`. Reference the summary going forward — never re-process the original.
- **Save research, don't repeat it** — before researching a topic, check if `docs/plans/` already has a plan doc for it. Read it instead of re-searching.

## Documentation Rules

- `docs/arch.md` is the primary context file for this workspace — keep it **token-optimized for LLMs**
- Tables over prose, self-contained sections, grep-friendly headings
- Under 300 lines — link to project-specific docs for details
- Feature docs (`docs/features/*.md`) can be verbose — they're for deep dives

## Skills Convention

All projects use a standard skill/command pattern:

| Format | Use When | Example |
|--------|----------|---------|
| **Skill** (`skills/name/SKILL.md`) | Core workflow skills needing `allowed-tools` control | startnow, updatenow, advise, l3, audit, localcompact |
| **Command** (`commands/name.md`) | Project-specific domain commands | build-api, gen-tests, review |

**Core skills** (always skill format with YAML frontmatter):

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `/startnow` | Load project/workspace context at session start |
| `/updatenow` | Update docs after changes |
| `/advise` | Research + recommend (customized per project domain) |
| `/l3` | Debug/investigate issues |
| `/audit` | Project health check (security, cost, performance, quality) |
| `/localcompact` | Compact arch.md back under 300 lines |
| `/newproject` | Scaffold a new project folder with all standard files and skills |

**Scaffolding new projects:** See `docs/plans/new-project-checklist.md`

## Workspace-Level Rules

- **Don't initialize git at this level** — each project manages its own git repo
- When organizing or moving projects, always verify git repos still work after the move
- Cross-project concerns (shared patterns, common configs) go in `docs/` at this level
